script: var d = new Date(4132517400000); (Date.UTC(d.getFullYear(), d.getMonth(), d.getDate(), d.getHours(), d.getMinutes(), d.getSeconds(), d.getMilliseconds()) - d.getTime()) / 60000 === -d.getTimezoneOffset()
note: the local fields are LocalTime(t)'s and the offset is (t - LocalTime(t)) / msPerMinute, in every zone
since: 14

id: date/to-string/0717
area: date
op: toString and the local fields agree
in: f64:0x428E1169DA6E0000
out: value: bool:true
class: normative
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-todatestring spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-localtime spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-timezoneestring spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-date.prototype.gettimezoneoffset ref:dateref@1
script: var d = new Date(4132517400000); var p = function (n) { return (n < 10 ? "0" : "") + n; }; var m = / ([0-9]{2}):([0-9]{2}):([0-9]{2}) GMT([+-])([0-9]{2})([0-9]{2})/.exec(d.toString()); m[1] + m[2] + m[3] === p(d.getHours()) + p(d.getMinutes()) + p(d.getSeconds()) && (m[4] === "-" ? 1 : -1) * (m[5] * 60 + m[6] * 1) === d.getTimezoneOffset()
note: toString's clock and offset are LocalTime(t)'s and the zone's at t, in every zone with whole-minute offsets, which every zone has after 1979
since: 14

